<h2>I'm Alex</h2>
<figure class="portrait">
  <img src="AL_headshot.jpeg" alt="Headshot of Alex Legault" width="200" height="200">
</figure>
<p>I like building and learning. I get to do both of those things through a career in product management. For the past decade+, I've been leading product teams at <a href="https://pitchbook.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PitchBook Data</a> and <a href="https://carta.com/venture-capital/fund-administration/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Carta- Fund Admin</a> building for private markets investors. My "sweet spot" has been joining teams in the 10-15M ARR range and scaling them to 9 figures. Currently, I serve as General Manager at <a href="https://lumonic.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lumonic</a> leading Product, Implementations, and Customer Success to see if I can take a company from 100k in ARR to 9 figures.</p>
<p>Prior, I worked at early stage stage startups in Seattle and more traditional companies like State Farm in a marketing capacity.</p>
<p>My degree is in psychology from the University of Washington where I focused on what influences which neural pathways are used in moral decision-making as well as sports psychology. For fun, I also spent a year living in Bogota, Colombia meeting family and improving my spanish.</p>
<p>Beyond the office, I build and learn through hobbies like reading, fishing, hunting, skiing, and flying. I use this website as a sort of diary that has the added benefit of letting other people get to know me.</p>
<p>You can reach me on LinkedIn or at hello at alexlegault.com. Things I would be happy if you contacted me about:</p>
<ul>
  <li>How to break into Product Management</li>
  <li>Forming peer groups with Seattle-based product leaders</li>
  <li>Improving Seattle tech/startup ecosystem</li>
